     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Verdana,Arial,Helvetica;font-size:12.8px\">I have a multi-level example where I expect the relationship between two individual-level variables to be moderated by a group-level variable (one that varies only between-groups). Can I test this hypothesis using lavaan?</span></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>No, lavaan does not yet allow level-1 slopes/correlations to be random across level-2 units.  Only intercepts are random.</div><div><br></div><div><div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422693224000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2fxuOcgqN-upJoHy4HAuJl\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div></div><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ]
